The verifier error occurs because `helper_a` is considered a sleepable function due to its call to `bpf_copy_from_user`, and it is invoked within an IRQ-disabled region created by `bpf_local_irq_save` and `bpf_local_irq_restore`. Sleepable functions cannot be called in IRQ-disabled contexts.

The simplest fix is to move the call to `helper_a` outside the IRQ-disabled section, either before `bpf_local_irq_save` or after `bpf_local_irq_restore`. The patch below places it after the restore to maintain the original order of operations as closely as possible.

```diff
--- a/case.c
+++ b/case.c
@@ -494,9 +494,9 @@ int __noinline helper_a(int i)
 SEC("?syscall")
 int entry(void *ctx)
 {
 	unsigned long flags;

 	bpf_local_irq_save(&flags);
-	helper_a(0);
 	bpf_local_irq_restore(&flags);
+	helper_a(0);
 	return 0;
 }
```

This change ensures `helper_a` is no longer inside the IRQ-disabled region, satisfying the verifier's execution context safety requirements.
